# EcoPunto product UI = Apple feel

The product (`/app` and future app chrome) should feel like an Apple interface: direct, interruptible, materials, spatial. Keep pine `#2F7050` and petroleum `#0A3D4A` — do not clone iOS blue or San Francisco.

The marketing landing (`app/landing.tsx`) stays editorial (Instrument Serif, grain, zig-zag). Do not restyle it into Settings.app.

When building or reviewing product UI / motion, read and follow:

- `.cursor/skills/apple-design/SKILL.md`
- `.cursor/skills/animate/SKILL.md` for new motion
- `.cursor/skills/review-animations/SKILL.md` when auditing motion

Hard rules on product surfaces:

- Feedback on pointer-down (`active:scale-[0.97]`, ~100ms), not on click
- `transform` / `opacity` only; never `scale(0)` or `ease-in` on enter
- UI motion under 300ms; springs for anything the user can grab
- Translucent chrome (`liquid-glass`) with content scrolling underneath
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and `prefers-reduced-transparency`
- Grouped lists, large titles, continuous corners
- Every screen answers: where am I, where can I go, how do I leave
